; Fleet formatting rules — THE source of truth for every adopted repo.
; Sync law: this file is copied byte-identical to .cljfmt.edn in each
; repo. The CI gate (cljfmt check), the editor (Calva / clojure-lsp),
; and the agent write-hook (clojure-mcp-light) all read the repo copy,
; so system-wide rules and edit-local rules are the same file by
; construction. Changes happen HERE, by a fleet-level commit, and are
; then propagated to the repos — a repo-local edit to .cljfmt.edn is
; drift and fails the fleet config-diff check.
; v1 was the cljfmt defaults plus ns sorting; v2 (Phase 1 retro,
; cohost-media-example): :sort-ns-references? is FALSE — sorting
; :require lists reorders namespace load order, which is semantics,
; not formatting; the media demo broke on it (proven by a
; reader-normalized form-tree diff: require order was the only
; difference). Every non-default entry below is earned by a retro
; and recorded here with its reason.
; v2 correction (Phase 2, Eve lane, 2026-11-22): there is NO
; :indents entry. An :indents key in .cljfmt.edn REPLACES cljfmt
; 0.16.6's built-in indent table in the standalone loader (it does
; not merge), so the v1/v2 `:indents {}` silently dropped every
; default rule — defn/ns bodies came out aligned under their first
; argument instead of block-indented. Measured on one Eve file:
; 2089 diff lines with `:indents {}` vs 111 under the defaults.
; Trees formatted while `:indents {}` was in force carry that
; alignment style and need one `cljfmt fix` after this correction
; propagates. To add a fleet indent rule, write the FULL merged
; table or use :extra-indents — never a bare :indents map.
{:remove-surrounding-whitespace? true
 :remove-trailing-whitespace? true
 :remove-consecutive-blank-lines? true
 :insert-missing-whitespace? true
 :sort-ns-references? false
 :align-associative? false}
